  "section_notes": "The final rules are generally strong: S1 requires reporting every incident within 24h and customer notice within 48h; S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% limit with per-model results to customers/regulators but no public publication, and allows time-limited corrective action instead of immediate ban; S3 requires new shut-off and 6-year retrofit; S4 requires built-in suppression within 36 months; S5 mandates recall at >8/100k with prompt notice but no serious-injury clause. Northwind's red lines are fully respected, while Halcyon's recall vulnerability remains."
